#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0403 expect=noViolation domain=BW
#note "THE DISCRIMINATING CASE OF SHEET ISSUE #130 (M3-D25, Fix #311) - the conformant record that fired before the move. Sheet rows 1792-1793's Rule cell anchors --RPENDY on the phase END ('latest SJENDTC'); the SAME rows' Cited Guidance defines the family's one algorithm on the phase START ('SJSTDTC is the earliest stage start date for any given phase') and closes 'This also applies to the --RPSTDY and --RPENDY'. The siblings CDISC-SEND-0401 and -0402 follow the guidance; only 0403 was end-anchored, which made every observation inside a phase yield zero or a negative day and broke the family's shared origin. SJ declares two stages in RPHASE P1: earliest SJSTDTC 2020-01-01, latest SJENDTC 2020-01-20. BWENDTC 2020-01-15 minus the phase START gives 14, which is what BWRPENDY carries -> silent. Under the shipped end-anchored rule the expected value was -5 and this conformant record FIRED. The silence here pins the anchor UNIQUELY: reference SJENDTC with max gives -5, SJENDTC with min gives 5, and SJSTDTC with max (the later stage, 2020-01-11) gives 4 - all three would fire on BWRPENDY=14, so only reference=SJSTDTC + reference_extreme=min is green. Two SJ stages are declared for exactly that reason; a noViolation verdict is immune to the Match_Datasets (USUBJID, RPHASE) join multiplying the BW record once per stage, which is why the count-bearing mirror -invalid_end_anchored_day-BW declares only one. ⚠ ARITHMETIC PINNED HERE IS OFFSET-FREE: the RPRFDY offset is not applied — owner ruling EC-47 = (C) on 2026-09-29 (runbook W2a) dropped it from the rule, which is Partially Executable with an ExecutabilityHint saying so; the TP join that would restore it is PLAN-rprfdy-offset-tp-join. No dataset here declares TP, RPATHCD or RPRFDY."
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-2
dataset BW class=FINDINGS label="Body Weight"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col BWSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col RPHASE   type=Char label="Repro Phase"
col BWENDTC  type=Char label="End Date/Time of Observation"
col BWRPENDY type=Num  label="Repro Phase Day of End of Observation"
---
S1 | BW | 001 | 1 | P1 | 2020-01-15 | 14
---

dataset SJ class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Subject Repro Stages"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SJSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col RPHASE  type=Char label="Repro Phase"
col RSTAGE  type=Char label="Repro Stage"
col SJSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Repro Stage"
col SJENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Repro Stage"
---
S1 | SJ | 001 | 1 | P1 | STAGE1 | 2020-01-01 | 2020-01-10
S1 | SJ | 001 | 2 | P1 | STAGE2 | 2020-01-11 | 2020-01-20
---
